{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3336","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3336","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3336\",\"parent_revision\":\"5d6450b0fd59001dadc9cc76f54ede5e88190b4ba408bdb82972ac8b49189641\",\"root_revision\":\"5d6450b0fd59001dadc9cc76f54ede5e88190b4ba408bdb82972ac8b49189641\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Chore\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-29\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe root cause behind #3329's deletion, generalized: `skills/backlog/SKILL.md` re-explained MCP tool parameters and return shapes in hand-written prose that the tool's own docstring/`Field(description=...)` annotations already stated \u2014 and that duplicate was structurally guaranteed to drift, because FastMCP regenerates the live tool schema from the code every server start, while a prose copy in a skill file changes only when someone remembers to edit it. That mechanism is what produced the deleted skill's \\\"12 tools\\\" heading against 28 real ones, a dead storage-format claim, and a broken `fastmcp` invocation example.\\n\\nConfirmed during #3329 this isn't unique to that one skill: `plugins/development-harness/README.md`'s \\\"Core backlog tools\\\" table has the identical shape (filed separately as #3335).\\n\\nGoal: audit other `dh:*` skills for the same pattern \u2014 prose that restates an MCP tool's parameters, return fields, or behavior, checkable live against the tool's actual schema via `ToolSearch`. Where found: delete the restatement from the skill, and if a genuine content gap exists, add it to the tool's own docstring instead (verified in #3329 to be the correct destination \u2014 it's literally the schema the agent is shown when deciding how to call the tool, a stronger and self-maintaining hook that a skill-file restatement can never be).\\n\\nUser-provided context: see #3329 for the full investigation this generalizes from, including three concrete examples where this exact check (comparing a doc's claim against the live `ToolSearch` schema) revealed the doc was either already redundant or actively wrong.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Follow-up from #3329 (dh:backlog dead-skill cleanup)\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-29\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"f9650c84a2a5f857d34d6274b55a19e7466dee98cef45c5156fe3f2ba7b33e97\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABReqIMQ\"}"}